HEADLINE
==============================================================================
  The CERTIFIABLE figure is on the uncapped subset (Z* fully enumerated):
    Gate-3 / all decisions:          3.4% (uncapped)   vs  4.9% (all, capped-contaminated)
    Gate-3 / (clean+Gate-3) [O-inv]: 4.4% (uncapped)   vs  6.3% (all)
    clean (free labels): 1423/1924 = 74.0% (uncapped)

  The CAP bites hardest inside the explosive HR clusters -- exactly where
  C-MeT label-symmetry (Gate-3) lives. So the capped-contaminated 'all'
  figure is NOT a random-slice estimate; the uncapped subset is the honest one.

  O-DEPENDENCE (alphabet-only prior run, all 32 capped): Gate-2 exploded
  2613 -> 28138 (~10x) while Gate-3 stayed chemistry-bounded. Gate-2 is
  combinatorial in the grammar; Gate-3 is an O-invariant of the chemistry.
  => the Gate-3 / (clean+Gate-3) ratio is the O-stable denominator; the raw
  Gate-3 / all-decisions fraction drifts with whatever O you ran at.

  TWO INDEPENDENT RESULTS, kept in separate sentences:
  (1) THINNESS: the conformational frontier is a small fraction of decisions.
  (2) SOLVABILITY: whether that thin frontier is simulable (AF2/MD) or
      measurable-only (cryo-EM) is the citrinin hinge experiment, unsettled.
  A 5% frontier that needs cryo-EM is still a wall, just a thin one. Thinness
  sized != biology delivered.
